<p><a href="/work-preview/">← Selected work</a></p>

<p>
  I’ve been a senior UX designer at Red Hat since 2021, based in Vermont and working on enterprise
  digital platforms—first redhat.com, now primarily docs.redhat.com. The work is systems-heavy: big
  catalogs, embedded engineers, content strategists, and surfaces that have to hold up for years.
</p>

<p>Three chapters so far:</p>

<h2><a href="/work-preview/red-hat/redhat-com/">rHomepage, nav, and research</a></h2>
<p>
  Projects for redhat.com: simplifying the homepage, redesigning primary navigation away from a “wall of products,” refreshing page templates, and co-leading in-person research with users.
</p>

<h2><a href="/work-preview/red-hat/unified-learn/">Docs & learning</a></h2>
<p>
  Led design maintenance and upgrades for the documentation platform (~55k weekday visitors). It's grown beyond docs into a more general learning destination, with more learning contnet types planned to migrate.
</p>

<h2><a href="/work-preview/red-hat/docs-feedback/">On-page feedback</a></h2>
<p>
  Grass-roots PWDR (people who do research) work from 2022 to 2024 helped me three years of direct user research at our yearly conference. I co-led the push for an evergreen on-page feedback mechanism on the docs experience, which the team is still iterating on today.
</p>
